\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
For every fixed rational $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, is there one randomized logarithmic-word RAM algorithm returning a $(1+\varepsilon )-multiplicative$ upper estimate of ordinary string edit distance with probability $\geq 2/3$ and worst-case expected running time $N^{1+o(1)}$ in total string length N, including all preprocessing, with exact zero output on equal strings?

\subsection{Short English statement}
For every fixed rational $\varepsilon \in (0,1)$, is there one randomized logarithmic-word RAM algorithm returning a $(1+\varepsilon )-multiplicative$ upper estimate of ordinary string edit distance with probability $\geq 2/3$ and worst-case expected running time $N^{1+o(1)}$ in total string length N, including all preprocessing, with exact zero output on equal strings?

\subsection{Sources}
\begin{itemize}
\item[S1] OpenAI, manuscript citation page. Source of the formulation motivating this local problem.
